From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:15:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/52] Issue sim-script stop/pause/kill orders without a
 command-stream id check

IssueStop, IssuePause, IssueKillSelf and IssueDestroySelf (0x006F1AB0,
0x006F1C50, 0x006F6F50, 0x006F70D0) build their issue data and call
UNIT_IssueCommand (0x006F12C0) directly, like every other sim-script
Issue* function. The rebuild sent them through Sim::IssueCommand, the
command-stream entry point, whose ValidateNewCommandId checks the
network command id against the current command source. A script order
carries no id (0xFFFFFFFF), so every one was dropped:

  IssueCommand: ignoring issue of cmd id 0xffffffff from <player>
  because the id's source (255) is wrong (should be 0)

650-900 times per skirmish, mostly FAF's AI (platoons, engineers and
transports stopping units) and CommandUnit.OnStartBuild; none of those
units ever stopped, paused or self-destructed on script request.

CUnitUnloadUnits::TaskTick had the same mistake for the move it gives
units unloaded by a staging platform or a stationary transport
(0x006269FC: UNIT_IssueCommand(sim, detached, issueData, clear = 1)).

(cherry picked from commit ea92757a580669212c9bfe47cceb76acaa046f1c)

Ported onto 8977bb9d: upstream rewrote the selection helpers next to the deleted BuildSelectedEntitySetFromUnits; only the helper is removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 91c8b8120c18b3857ba7bdea85f163004e938dc3)

Ported onto 13ce9e55: upstream 132819e1 folded SEntitySetTemplateUnit/ArmyUnitSet into EntitySetTemplate<Unit>; the selections are built with its copy constructor and Add.
